       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum for metformin. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, given as 850 mg three times daily with meals. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, for 2,550 mg/day. This is the maximum for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose.** If you intended something else, give me the dose and frequency.\n\nIf you really do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and include a note on the order about the clinical rationale. I'd still advise checking with pharmacy first."
      }
